<% content_for :title, "Libraries" %>
<div class="doc max-w-4xl space-y-12">
  <header>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Libraries and integrations</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg">The fastest way to start: drop in a small client instead of writing HTTP calls yourself. They're open source, have no dependencies, and handle errors the same way everywhere. Prefer to call the API directly? See the <%= link_to "API docs", docs_path, class: "text-blue underline" %>.</p>
    <% unless OpenTrust::SDKS_PUBLISHED %>
      <p class="mt-4 rounded-md border border-amber bg-amber-wash p-3 text-sm">The Ruby and Node packages are about to be published. Until they are, call the API directly with any HTTP client.</p>
    <% end %>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Official libraries</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="card">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Ruby</h3><span class="tag border-line text-ink-soft">gem · v0.1</span></div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm">Works with Rails, Sinatra or plain Ruby 2.7+.</p>
        <div class="codeblock mt-4"><div class="codeblock-bar">install</div><pre><code>gem install opentrust
# or in your Gemfile
gem "opentrust"</code></pre></div>
        <div class="codeblock mt-3"><div class="codeblock-bar">use</div><pre><code>client = OpenTrust::Client.new
# reads OPENTRUST_API_KEY

result = client.lookup(order.phone)
flag_for_review(order) if result.reported?</code></pre></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Node.js</h3><span class="tag border-line text-ink-soft">npm · v0.1</span></div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm">Node 18+, ES modules, TypeScript types included.</p>
        <div class="codeblock mt-4"><div class="codeblock-bar">install</div><pre><code>npm install opentrust</code></pre></div>
        <div class="codeblock mt-3"><div class="codeblock-bar">use</div><pre><code>import { OpenTrust } from "opentrust";

const ot = new OpenTrust();
// reads OPENTRUST_API_KEY

const result = await ot.lookup(order.phone);
if (result.reported) flagForReview(order);</code></pre></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">What every library does</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li><strong>Same four calls:</strong> check one number, check many (up to 100), share an experience, and see your remaining checks.</li>
      <li><strong>Typed errors:</strong> a missing key, no checks left, a duplicate report, a bad number and a rate limit each raise their own error, so you can handle them directly.</li>
      <li><strong>Short timeouts:</strong> 5 seconds by default, so a slow response never holds up your checkout.</li>
      <li><strong>The notice travels with the result:</strong> every result carries the reminder that reports are unverified observations. Please show it to anyone who sees a result.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 font-bold">Please don't block checkout on OpenTrust</p>
    <p class="mt-1">Use results as one input, have a person review decisions that matter, and carry on if OpenTrust can't be reached:</p>
    <div class="codeblock mt-3"><div class="codeblock-bar">fail open</div><pre><code>begin
  result = client.lookup(order.phone)
  flag_for_review(order) if result.reported?
rescue OpenTrust::Error => e
  logger.warn("OpenTrust unavailable: #{e.message}") # carry on
end</code></pre></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">On the way</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">Most Indian online stores run on a platform, so we're starting there. Each will check the billing number at checkout and flag the order for review, rather than blocking it.</p>
    <ul class="mt-4 divide-y divide-ink/10 rounded-lg border border-line bg-white">
      <% [["WooCommerce", "Plugin for WordPress stores", "In testing"], ["Shopify", "App for Shopify stores", "In development"], ["Python", "Package for Django, Flask and scripts", "Planned"], ["PHP", "Package for Laravel and plain PHP", "Planned"]].each do |name, desc, status| %>
        <li class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 px-4 py-3"><div><span class="font-bold"><%= name %></span> <span class="text-sm text-ink-soft">· <%= desc %></span></div><span class="tag <%= status == "Planned" ? "border-line text-ink-soft" : "border-sun-deep bg-white text-ink" %>"><%= status %></span></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4">Using something else, or want to help build one? <%= mail_to OpenTrust::FEEDBACK_EMAIL, "Tell us", class: "text-blue underline" %><% if OpenTrust::REPO_URL %>, or send a pull request to our <%= link_to "public repository", OpenTrust::REPO_URL, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "text-blue underline" %><% end %>.</p>
  </section>
</div>
